lessons.notes:
## for

```java
for (int i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
    System.out.print(i + " ");     // 0 1 2 3 4
}
for (int i = 10; i > 0; i -= 3) {
    System.out.print(i + " ");     // 10 7 4 1
}
```

The variable `i` exists only inside the loop.

## while and do-while

```java
int countdown = 3;
while (countdown > 0) {
    System.out.println(countdown--);
}

int choice;
do {
    choice = sc.nextInt();
} while (choice < 1 || choice > 3);
```

## break, continue and labels

```java
outer:
for (int r = 0; r < 5; r++) {
    for (int c = 0; c < 5; c++) {
        if (r * c > 6) break outer;   // leaves both loops
    }
}
```

## Nested loops

```java
for (int r = 1; r <= 3; r++) {
    for (int c = 1; c <= 3; c++) {
        System.out.print(r * c + "\t");
    }
    System.out.println();
}
```

## Common patterns

- **Sum**: `total += x;`
- **Count**: `if (cond) count++;`
- **Max**: `if (x > best) best = x;`

## Pitfalls

- **Off by one**: `i <= n` vs `i < n`.
- **Infinite loops**: the condition never becomes false.
- **Integer overflow**: sums of many ints may need `long`.

